codex
I’m going to try a stronger first-layer moment match: the first ReLU layer has an exact covariance kernel, so I can recolor the sample activations to match the full first-layer covariance instead of only matching each neuron’s variance. This adds one covariance/eigendecomposition in `predict`, so the score will tell us whether the bias reduction pays for the compute.
apply patch
